# Agent rules for this repo

Before building scenes, editing the script map, rendering, or muxing, follow **`docs/instructions.md`** as your system prompt.

Process lineage: same hard rules as video 2 (`../../../ai-image-explainer/docs/instructions.md`) and the video-1 repo  
[`../../../1-hour-challenge/docs/instructions.md`](../../../1-hour-challenge/docs/instructions.md)  
(and launch lessons in that repo’s `docs/launch_analytics_notes.md`).

Hard rules:

1. **`docs/script_visual_map.md` is the contract** — do not invent on-screen labels/numbers outside it.
2. **Bit workflow:** Arabic paragraph (Ali) → agent proposes animation → Ali **approves** → only then write Manim. Never code a new bit before approval.
3. After a useful render, export ~8–12 frames to `keyframes/<segment_id>/` via `scripts/export_keyframes.py`.
4. Preview render by default; HD only when Ali asks. Skip-up-to-date render/mux is default; `--force` rebuilds.
5. Do not import or depend on `1-hour-challenge/our_scenes` at runtime — copy/adapt helpers into this repo if needed.
